{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "075T", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\pi : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-gerbe-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:239310fd32d4da9f64597d8fb94e747732e50fbec67dc8e29b8d71856e5ddd8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:76e3a4ad4c78cf0a5e48667fcbf0bab54c38ff45460f0792c3e8f0c25939f6d0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nIf <MATH_0002> is a gerbe over <MATH_0003>, then <MATH_0004> is surjective\nand smooth.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f71f2ac9b401daac29ad14da1d29068decbcbf67c7f9da7a8debe68d4ff51cbf", "unit_id": "tag:0DN8:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "075T", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}' \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y} = U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} = [U/G]$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$G \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-fppf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-descent-smooth}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-local-structure-gerbe}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-quotient-stack}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fc7e51e7b48d3470197a426dca9f0847b8264d9ca3c1c0317da7d6661b766e53", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3679145530a2aae4c8d1b5f1bf1c3b439354b34ab0c08fe25cc15f6a8c37c574", "source_text": "We have seen surjectivity in Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002>\nit suffices to prove to the lemma after replacing <MATH_0001> by a base change\nwith a surjective, flat, locally finitely presented morphism\n<MATH_0002>. By\nLemma <REF_0003>\nwe may assume <MATH_0003> is an algebraic space and\n<MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005> with <MATH_0006> flat and\nlocally of finite presentation.\nThen we win by Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c5b0019e8a03f70f583bd629e1cb7ca38ef757c161943529c5242ea8105db5e2", "unit_id": "tag:0DN8:proof"}
